  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Departure Board",
    "overview": "Evertusk reads like a board in a quiet terminal: times in a narrow column, one lit lamp for what is running, and rows ruled by hairlines. It sits beside an editor, often at night, so dark is the default and the near-black neutrals stay out of the way. Light and bright themes keep the same roles with new values.\n\nDensity is high and deliberate. A title bar sits over three panes: a rail, a board of same-height rows, and a session. The title bar's two toggles hide the rail and the board, so a session can take the whole window. Color carries meaning rather than decoration, and depth comes from small tonal steps and hairlines. Tool activity folds to a single line so prompts and answers read as the conversation.\n\nThe signature moment is small: when a running session changes, its time and prompt count turn over into place like a flap, beside a pulsing lamp. Under reduced motion the value simply updates and the lamp holds still.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Neutral near-black scale with one amber and one failure red.",
      "The system font for everything; tabular numerals wherever numbers line up.",
      "Hairline-ruled rows on fixed columns.",
      "Tonal layering; shadows only on what floats.",
      "Compact 12px to 14px working type. Nothing goes below 12px.",
      "Your prompts sit in a bubble on the right; the agent's answers run plain on the left."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Three Meanings Rule",
        "body": "Amber means selection, running and saved, and nothing else. Focus and search hits count as selection. The elephant mark is amber because it is the brand, not because it signals.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Red Is Failure Rule",
        "body": "Red marks something that failed. A count of failures may be red; a merely large number may not.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Same Roles Rule",
        "body": "Themes change values, never roles. Components read theme tokens, so new work holds up in dark, light and bright. Only code surfaces stay constant.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The 12px Floor Rule",
        "body": "No text goes below 12px, in any theme or at any window size.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Face Rule",
        "body": "Don't add a display or condensed face for numerals. Totals stand out through weight and colour, and they line up through tabular figures.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Straight Column Rule",
        "body": "Anything repeated on the board shares a column edge. A new datum goes in the meta line, not a new column that breaks the run.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Board Rule",
        "body": "Nothing resting in the three panes casts a shadow. If something needs lifting, step its tone.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** read color from theme tokens, so every new surface works in dark, light and bright.",
      "**Do** keep amber to selection, running and saved, including focus and search hits as selection.",
      "**Do** set times and counts in the system font with tabular numerals, at 12px or above.",
      "**Do** rule board rows with a 1px hairline on the fixed 72px, 48px and flexible columns.",
      "**Do** show state with a neutral fill first: hover graphite, then selected graphite.",
      "**Do** fold tool activity to one line and keep the raw record one step away.",
      "**Do** pair animation with a plain update under `prefers-reduced-motion`.",
      "**Do** keep code surfaces dark in every theme."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** use amber for links, callouts, decoration or emphasis.",
      "**Don't** use red for anything that hasn't failed.",
      "**Don't** add a display or condensed face, or bundle a font.",
      "**Don't** set any text below 12px.",
      "**Don't** add shadows to anything resting in the three panes.",
      "**Don't** convey tool or status by color alone; pair it with a label, count or lamp.",
      "**Don't** add a new accent hue to distinguish a block or tool.",
      "**Don't** add a board column or let rows vary in height outside search results and bookmarks."
    ]
  }
